WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.297
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:03.994 --> 00:00:05.410
SPEAKER: Welcome
to the Quickstart

00:00:05.410 --> 00:00:08.620
for Google Cloud
Persistent Disks.

00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:12.040
From the VM Instance
page, select your instance

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:14.170
by clicking on its name.

00:00:14.170 --> 00:00:18.010
In the VM Instance
Details page, select Edit.

00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:22.300
Scroll down to the
Additional Disk section.

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:25.180
And then click Add Item.

00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:28.480
Click on the name
and create disk.

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:33.370
In the new dialog that shows
up, enter new-disk for the name

00:00:33.370 --> 00:00:37.390
and change the disk type to
Standard persistent disk.

00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:41.830
Under Source Type,
select none (blank disk)

00:00:41.830 --> 00:00:45.010
and then set the size to 500 GB.

00:00:45.010 --> 00:00:46.210
Click Create.

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:49.120
Now back to the VM
Instance Details page,

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:52.870
you will have to scroll
down and then select Save.

00:00:52.870 --> 00:00:54.880
We will now confirm
the persistent disk

00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:56.050
has been created.

00:00:56.050 --> 00:01:00.640
To do that click, SSH to
connect to the new SSH terminal.

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:03.140
It may take some time
to connect sometimes.

00:01:03.140 --> 00:01:10.210
But once it connects, let's
type in sudo lsblk and then

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:27.550
the Command sudo mkfs.ext4 -m
0 -F -E lazy_itable_init=0,

00:01:27.550 --> 00:01:34.760
lazy_journal_init=0,
discard /dev/sdb.

00:01:37.540 --> 00:01:40.570
This will format
the attached disk,

00:01:40.570 --> 00:01:45.220
and you will see the inode
tables that are writing.

00:01:45.220 --> 00:01:48.250
Now note, this may
take a little bit long.

00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:50.950
So we will wait
for it to format.

00:01:50.950 --> 00:01:53.140
Almost there.

00:01:53.140 --> 00:01:57.220
Once it's done formatting, you
can create a mount directory

00:01:57.220 --> 00:02:03.510
with this command sudo mkdir
-p /mnt/disk/mymountdir.

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:14.980
And then mount it with this
command sudo mount -0 discard,

00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:21.010
defaults /dev/sdb
/mount/disk/mymountdir.

00:02:25.030 --> 00:02:31.510
Finally, change the permissions
on the disk by using sudo chmod

00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:34.630
a+w on the mount directory.

00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:36.130
Well, congratulations.

00:02:36.130 --> 00:02:39.010
You've completed
this Quickstart.

